    "note": "The thermal rms sensor and amplitude control loop — the accuracy of the whole module. U1 is the thermal converter: it puts out a dc voltage equal to the rms value of the amplifier output applied to it, available at TP1. U2A integrates that, and U2B with U3 and U12A form a square-root amplifier that keeps the sensor's settling time constant across the range. U5 buffers the result. Below 11 kHz K2A switches C7 in for extra low-frequency filtering. From 12 kHz to 1.1 MHz K10 in the set position sends the buffered output to the RCL line for A11's adc; from 1.2 MHz to 30 MHz U12B compares it against DAC OUT (which K11 makes by tying DAC OUT HI and DAC SENSE HI together) and the difference leaves as the WB AMPLITUDE CONTROL line to A6.",
